.TH GIT-TWIG 1 "" "git-twig" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-twig \- lightweight Git worktrees using native copy-on-write
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git twig
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B git twig skill
.br
.B git twig -h
.br
.B git twig --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Twig creates ordinary linked Git worktrees. Supported creation requests use native
copy-on-write on macOS/APFS, Linux reflink filesystems, or Windows ReFS.
Other requests use
Git's worktree implementation, without inheriting local or ignored files.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new [-b branch | --detach] path [commit]
Create a worktree. Native copying requires the source checkout's current HEAD;
other commits and unsupported options delegate to Git.
.TP
.B list [--porcelain [-z]]
List worktrees. Porcelain is Git's stable machine-readable format.
.TP
.B remove path
Remove a worktree and its registration. Check for changes before removing it.
.TP
.B move path new-path
Move a worktree and update its registration.
.TP
.B lock [--reason text] path
Protect registration from pruning, moving or removal. Does not lock file contents.
.TP
.B unlock path
Remove registration protection.
.TP
.B prune [--dry-run] [--expire time]
Remove stale registrations, not working directories. Preview with --dry-run.
.TP
.B repair [path ...]
Repair repository/worktree links after manual moves, not contents or conflicts.
.TP
.B skill
Print the bundled agent instructions, including the command reference.
.SH EXAMPLE
From the directory containing the source checkout named main:
.PP
.nf
git -C main twig new -b feat/x ../feat-x HEAD
.fi
.PP
The destination is resolved relative to main, so it is a sibling named feat-x.
HEAD must name the source checkout's current commit for native copying.
.SH CHECKOUT COVERAGE
Development builds support common LF policies such as text=auto eol=lf.
Private candidate bytes are compared to raw target blobs. Git materializes
files requiring conversion or whose bytes differ; other verified files retain
sharing. These improvements are not in the published v0.3.0 release.
External filters, ident expansion, working-tree encodings, conditional config
includes and relative attribute-file configuration delegate to stock Git.
Checkout configuration and external attributes must not change during creation.
.SH STAGING
Staging is stored under the common Git directory in twigs/staging. Successful
operations remove their own staging. Failed/interrupted attempts retain diagnostic
state; inspect reported paths and registrations before retrying or deleting.
Source, destination and Git metadata must share a clone-capable filesystem for
the native path; unsupported layouts delegate to Git.
.SH HELP
Short help works outside repositories:
.PP
.nf
git twig -h
git twig new --help
.fi
.PP
Git turns top-level git twig --help into this manual lookup. Homebrew installs
the manual; Cargo installations can use git twig -h or git-twig --help instead.
See git-worktree(1) for the complete delegated Git option reference.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TWIG_TRACE=1
Report native backend selection, verified file clone and Git-written counts,
staging and fallback reasons to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-worktree (1),
.BR git (1)
